1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,520
Demo complete. Every screen looks finished.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:09,840
None of that tells you whether the server checks who may see what.

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:22,180
Four layers: browser, session, API, database.

4
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:31,910
Alice requests her own project. 200 OK.

5
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:39,480
Controlled test: Alice requests Bob's project, 2002.

6
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:45,990
The vulnerable endpoint returns Bob's project. 200 OK.

7
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:50,060
Authenticated was mistaken for authorised.

8
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:55,020
The gate asks: does a user exist?

9
00:00:55,020 --> 00:01:01,390
It never asks: does this user own this resource?

10
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:09,270
Fix: resolve the user on the server, query by id AND owner.

11
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:14,520
No match: 404, whether absent or not hers.

12
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:21,970
Retest: Alice's project 200. Bob's project 404.

13
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:27,300
Client-side identity claims change nothing.

14
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:32,330
This fixes one read path, not the whole app.

15
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:36,810
A working interface is not an authorization test.
